{
 "comment": "How the builder compiles and links thp8.exe with the pinned zig (x86_64-windows-gnu = clang + mingw-w64 + libc++). Mirrors thp8-native CMakeLists.txt. {lift} = <install>/.build/lift, {ps3recomp} / {title} = folders of this builder package. Notes (toolchain study 2026-10-05): zig maps -O1/-O2/-O3 to clang -O2, so '-O2 -Xclang -O3' gives the cc1 -O3 that clang-cl /O2 uses; zig defaults to -g -gcodeview and -fno-omit-frame-pointer; -fno-auto-import avoids a .refptr indirection on every extern (vm_base) access; each TU also gets -Xclang -object-file-name=<stable name> so objects are deterministic; PS3RECOMP_NO_NPDRM_KEYS keeps platform keys out of every build. THP8_RUNTIME_SPU_DEFAULTS=1 mirrors the CMake option (default ON since ps3recomp thp8-next3: the runtime has the spucheck SPU defaults, so the title stops setting them). 'options' mirror THP8_LIFT_FMA (-mfma on the lifted tree + -DTHP8_LIFT_FMA=1 everywhere; chosen per player CPU by the builder) and THP8_LIFT_MEMV (default on; off = -DPPU_MEMV= on the lifted tree: a compile flag only, no relift). -Wno-everything + -Werror=unknown-attributes (not -w: -w also hides this error): clang for MinGW silently IGNORES __declspec(thread), turning thread-local variables into shared globals; an 'unknown attribute ignored' must stop the build.",
 "common": [
  "-target",
  "x86_64-windows-gnu",
  "-O2",
  "-Xclang",
  "-O3",
  "-g0",
  "-fomit-frame-pointer",
  "-Wno-everything",
  "-Werror=unknown-attributes",
  "-fno-sanitize=undefined",
  "-fno-strict-aliasing",
  "-ffp-contract=off",
  "-msse4.1",
  "-fno-auto-import",
  "-DNDEBUG",
  "-DPS3RECOMP_NO_NPDRM_KEYS",
  "-DTHP8_RUNTIME_SPU_DEFAULTS=1",
  "-ffile-prefix-map={lift}=lift",
  "-ffile-prefix-map={ps3recomp}=ps3recomp",
  "-ffile-prefix-map={title}=title"
 ],
